# mcp (the PyPI package, pulled in only as semgrep's own dependency —
# backend/mcp_server/ is this project's hand-rolled MCP server and never
# imports the `mcp` package). Same root cause, same conclusion
# .github/workflows/deps.yml's pip-audit step already documents and
# ignores (PYSEC-2026-3481/3482/3483, the PySec IDs for these same three
# advisories): semgrep>=1.173 ships a fixed mcp, but every release from
# 1.173 onward hard-pins pyjwt[crypto]~=2.13.0, which conflicts with this
# project's own pyjwt>=2.14 fix for GHSA-w6j9-cwv2-h6wq — installing both
# is ResolutionImpossible. Each of these three requires an opt-in mcp
# server feature (experimental task handlers, an HTTP transport with
# bearer auth, or the deprecated WebSocket transport) that semgrep's own
# CLI-subprocess usage here never reaches. Revisit together with that
# pip-audit ignore list, not separately.
#
# Added 2026-10-09.
CVE-2026-52869
CVE-2026-52870
CVE-2026-59950
